# Another Chance ({2}{B} instant): "You may mill two cards. Then return up to two creature cards from your graveyard to your hand." Bot1 accepts, so Ornithopter and Phyrexian
# Walker are milled first (CR 701.17a) and, only because the milling comes first, are in the graveyard to be returned (the graveyard holds no creature card before); both go back
# to the hand - two, the most "up to two" allows. Black Lotus, sacrificed for the mana and so also in the graveyard, is no creature card and cannot be chosen.
